Design details:

**Doc order determination**: Build map doc → first entry seq (min seq among entries with that doc id). Docs eligible as boundaries: those that have ≥1 entry in store.entries. That covers in/out/transfer/count/arrival/return and reversals with entries (in-rev, out-rev, transfer-rev, count-rev, arrival-rev, return-rev). Cancel docs and cancel-reversals have no entries → rejected as boundary with clear message. Purchase ids: not in stock doc space; if the id matches a purchase only → "只有采购或取消记录的编号不可用" reject. If id matches both a purchase and a stock doc (same name allowed) → use the stock doc （同名采购不干扰）.

Boundary seq computation:
- fromDoc: period starts after the from-doc's last entry. So startSeq = max seq of from-doc entries (exclusive lower bound: entries with seq > fromEndSeq).
